title: "NovusLattice: Sutton-Chen Interatomic Potential in Sobolev H¹(Ω) Spaces & Industrial Continuum Mechanics"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
repository-code: "https://github.com/novomundus2-cmyk/NovusLattice"
license: "PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0"
keywords:
  - "computational physics"
  - "Sutton-Chen empirical potential"
  - "Sobolev spaces"
  - "FCC atomic lattice"
  - "sheet metal forming"
  - "elastic springback"
  - "industrial shearing"
  - "robotic tribology"
  - "thermal drift"
  - "multiscale modeling"
abstract: >-
  NovusLattice establishes a rigorous mathematical and computational bridge between 
  quantum-informed interatomic empirical potentials (Sutton-Chen model in FCC lattices) 
  and macroscale continuum deformation in Sobolev spaces H¹(Ω). The framework addresses 
  four mission-critical industrial manufacturing challenges: crystallographic shear in 
  cutting and punching, non-linear elastic springback recovery in high-precision sheet 
  bending (EPTA France benchmark, ±0.2 mm tolerance), asperity contact tribology in 
  robotic manipulation, and ambient factory floor thermal drift compensation.
